{"id":"6ccd47fd-0c96-4ba9-a91e-3fff3e7e4a05","object":"chat.completion","created":1784997979,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    tokens = list(case['tokens'])\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    # Sort calls by descending score, then ascending start, then call_id\\n    sorted_calls = sorted(calls, key=lambda c: (-c['score'], c['start'], c['call_id']))\\n    selected = []  # list of (start, end, call_id, replacement_tokens)\\n    intervals = []  # list of (start, end) for selected calls\\n    for c in sorted_calls:\\n        s, e = c['start'], c['end']\\n        # Check overlap with any selected interval\\n        overlap = False\\n        for sel_s, sel_e in intervals:\\n            if not (e <= sel_s or s >= sel_e):\\n                overlap = True\\n                break\\n        if not overlap:\\n            intervals.append((s, e))\\n            selected.append((s, e, c['call_id'], c['replacement_tokens']))\\n    # Order accepted calls by source start for reporting\\n    selected.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\\n    selected_call_ids = [x[2] for x in selected]\\n    # Apply replacements from right to left\\n    selected_for_replace = sorted(selected, key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\\n    for s, e, _, rep in selected_for_replace:\\n        tokens[s:e] = rep\\n    return {'selected_call_ids': selected_call_ids, 'tokens': tokens}\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for AGENT-TF-02. The case payload has tokens (list of strings) and calls (list of objects with call_id, start (int), end (int), score (float), replacement_tokens (list of strings)). The task: apply accepted API calls to text while preserving registered span order, rejecting overlaps, and keeping all eligible calls. The output must be {\"selected_call_ids\": list of strings, \"tokens\": list of strings}. The tokens are the interleaved token stream after applying replacements from selected calls.\n\nThe algorithm:\n- We have tokens list (original tokens).\n- For each call, we have start and end indices (0-based? The example shows start and end as indices into tokens? In the first case, tokens length 10, calls start 1, end 3 for call a, etc. Typically start inclusive, end exclusive. So call a covers tokens indices 1 and 2 (t1, t2). replacement_tokens is [\"<a>\"].\n- We need to select a subset of calls that do not overlap (non-overlapping spans), and we want to maximize some criteria? The instruction: \"Rank candidates by descending score, start position, then call ID. Greedily reject any span overlapping an already selected span.\" So we sort all calls by descending score, then ascending start? The phrase \"descending score, start position, then call ID.\" Typically means primary key descending score, secondary key ascending start position, tertiary key possibly ascending call ID (string). Then process in that order, and for each call, if its span does not overlap any already selected span, accept it. This is greedy selection.\n\n- Then order accepted calls by source start for reporting (so selected_call_ids should be in order of increasing start). Then apply replacements from right to left (i.e., process calls in descending order of start index) so that earlier offsets do not shift. For each accepted call in reverse start order, replace the token slice from start to end with the replacement_tokens list.\n\n- The final tokens list after all replacements becomes the output tokens.\n\nEdge cases: overlapping? The greedy selection ensures non-overlap. Also, note that indices are presumably non-negative and within token length. The call's end should be <= len(tokens). The start < end.\n\nThe output format: JSON object with keys selected_call_ids (list of strings) and tokens (list of strings). No additional keys.\n\nWe need to implement solve(case) in Python. The function receives the payload dict. It must return a dict with those keys.\n\nWe must